{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1374819-deviant-settings","id":1374819,"title":"Deviant settings.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-14T15:37:46-07:00","id":1374819,"title":"Deviant settings.","content":"I've gotten the idea to run a D:tR game for my players, and basically its a bunch of genotypals finally escaping their underground facility. I'm trying to figure out what what to have the &quot;surface&quot; be. I've had games like Bioshock, Prey, and Fallout run through my mind. I'm trying to go for an abandoned world feeling, like they were made to fight, or repopulate the world with superior forms. But I also want there to be a social aspect, like some cities are still around and well defended, or something. I've been toying around with aliens or zombies or something, but I can't quite put my finger on what's best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T16:53:11-07:00","id":1374830,"title":"","content":"You could go the Terminator route and have large portions of the world devastated by hostile AI","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T17:05:09-07:00","id":1374832,"title":"","content":"I think something like a pandemic or Contagion outbreak would work well for the feel you are trying to invoke without crossing the overused tropes of Zombies or trying to add aliens.<br /> <br /> Lots of death, paranoia and tribalism can occur if you trap people in a quarantine zone without adequate support for a n extended period of time.<br /> A disease that kills can leave ghosts without zombies. Heck you could even have it so if someone survives, they undergo the Divergence. A deadly disease that creates insane mutants out of those who survive it is reason enough for Conspiracies to be interested and authorities to lock down the area. Provides you with at least two groups of survivors that can exist in any given location too.<br /> <br /> Added bonus, it doesn't have to be a global catastrophe, so you can have an unaffected area the players discover later on if you want to change it up. Even if it is just the headquarters of another Conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T00:33:42-07:00","id":1375029,"title":"","content":"I'd like to avoid a straight up virus outbreak, considering the current climate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T02:12:25-07:00","id":1375042,"title":"","content":"Ghosts are one thing I'd go with, to create a sensation of a vanished human race but with things to talk to. Some sort of intelligent automaton is another idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T15:41:03-07:00","id":1375161,"title":"","content":"You could always just have them emerge somewhere with low population density, like rural Alaska or Siberia or the like. Alternatively, you could dig deep into the weird fiction <i>Deviant </i>draws on and have them turn out to be in the past or distant future (such as the burned-out Earth or Martian colonies suggested in <i>Mummy</i> 2e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T16:04:54-07:00","id":1375506,"title":"","content":"Hold up hold on just one bloody moment. Martian colonies in mummy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T17:31:35-07:00","id":1375519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1374819-deviant-settings?p=1375506#post1375506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hold up hold on just one bloody moment. Martian colonies in mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of Mummy 2e's sample story concepts concern the Fifth Sothic Turn in the 32nd century. One of the hooks is &quot;your meret wakes up in a small colony on Mars.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T17:59:47-07:00","id":1375521,"title":"","content":"There's also two sci-fi shards in VtR: Guide to the Night. Ascendancy is extremely cyberpunk while Night Without End is space opera. They're both just three pages long; half of which is geared towards vampires and the other half is mostly just general setting descriptors with a few plot hooks. Far from ready-to-use settings even for VtR games, but Night Without End may provide some inspiration. For example, barely inhabited planets, with the Deviant PCs caught between the untouched wilderness or exposure to alien environments, and the few colonies that have been set up and are probably rapidly expanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-18-2020, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T01:37:11-07:00","id":1375769,"title":"","content":"If time travel is an option, we could just dump the players in any sparely populated area in history. Turns out the Conspiracy is a God Machine cult who've suborned 'chronological load bearing' Infrastructure. It is a tad more Demon the Descent than I'd like for a new group hook, but if you want to avoid slapping together future settings...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T18:29:11-07:00","id":1377619,"title":"","content":"Watch the trailer for Ghostbusters Afterlife and read &quot;Earth, Air, Fire &amp; Water&quot; by Scott Cunningham. Your players were supposed to be obedient elemental soldiers, but the conspiracy that created them ran afoul of some Ghost Hunters. Your players emerge into what is left of the small town the two groups clashed in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:54:23-07:00","id":1381445,"title":"","content":"You could use the little used, real world version, that of a financial collapse. Think the Great Depression times ten.<br /> Cities are filled with empty, falling down buildings because the owners couldn't afford to keep them and no one has been maintaining them.<br /> Utilities are quickly becoming a thing of the past because no one is maintaining the infrastructure.<br /> Vast areas have little to no police presence due to a lack of resources, or the lack of interest by those who control those resources, and once Police services are gone the other emergency services soon follow as more and more places become lawless no-man's lands. If a crime is great enough to bring the police back into an area it comes with overwhelming force and little thought for collateral damage, then once the threat is dealt with they draw back to the places that still matter.<br /> For contrast in the middle of all of this detritus of society are the gleaming towers of wealthy gated communities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T02:24:32-07:00","id":1386937,"title":"","content":"Maybe a Tokyo Underground Situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12527-thearcane","name":"TheArcane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12527_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}